# Intent: The banner row and the subtitle strip, part 1 (owner decisions 2026-11-16). The screen has three fixed zones and nothing moves between them: the banner zone (y 0 to 28, reserved even when empty), the face zone (y 28 to 184) and the subtitle zone (y 184 to 240). The banner row is ONE rectangle, the same for every message (x 4, y 1, 312 by 26, radius 13): a leading icon, the text (a marquee only when it overflows the text area), a priority queue (privacy and remote cues first, then notices, then captions), a minimum display time of 1.5 s, auto-hide, replace-in-place tags, the violet remote session chip INSIDE the row (steady, text "Remote connected" and the controller label after it only when it has one, never redrawn on a heartbeat), and a small icon strip at the right for the always-on cues (microphone live, camera on, remote) and for battery and Wi-Fi only when something is wrong. The row fades in and out at full width over 150 ms; it never grows, shrinks or moves. The subtitle strip shows what the robot is saying at the bottom: no box, the build's own 20 px text font in white with a dark outline, at most two lines centered (one line in the middle of the zone), long sentences paged, a 150 ms fade, and it leaves 0.8 s after the robot stops talking. Pure logic and geometry live in hal/maipai_banner_core.h and hal/maipai_subs_core.h (host tested; the geometry is printed as the settings page table); the drawing is hal/maipai_banner.cc and hal/maipai_subtitles.cc on the top layer. The speech bubble gets a route hook so the avatar's words go to the subtitles or the banner. Cost: one 0.7 KB state in PSRAM and one 0.1 KB state, two timers (33 ms only while something shows, 100 ms otherwise); about 24 LVGL objects while the row shows and six while subtitles show, none when idle (deleted after 20 s and 5 s).
# Placement: unit (the banner runs on the robot, so it is complete with no host)
# Upstream: firmware/main/stackchan/avatar/skins/default/{default.h,speech_bubble.cpp} (ours, patch TA04); new files hal/maipai_banner_core.h, hal/maipai_banner.h, hal/maipai_banner.cc
# Check after a flash: self.remote.session active true shows the violet chip "Remote: connected" at the top and nothing at the bottom; self.remote.action shows its cue at the top; the face moves down and back without a jump; scripts/fw-serial.py snap of every style with a banner (host renderer PNGs under scripts/fw-face-render).

